{"url": "https://science-math.wright.edu/interdisciplinary-applied-science-and-mathematics-phd-program/admission", "final_url": "https://science-math.wright.edu/degrees-and-programs", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-28", "text": "Degrees and Programs | College of Science and Mathematics\nSkip to main content\nCollege of Science & Mathematics\nCalendar\nDirectories\nMaps\nPilot\nWINGS\nApply\nSearch Wright State\nSearch\nMenu\nClose\nMain navigation\nHome\nDegrees & Programs\nAdmission\nAdvising & Resources\nResearch\nExperiential Learning\nAlumni & Giving\nAbout\nSearch Wright State\nSearch\nDegrees & Programs\nAdmission\nAdvising & Resources\nResearch\nExperiential Learning\nAlumni & Giving\nAbout\nCalendar\nDirectories\nMaps\nPilot\nWINGS\nApply\nDegrees and Programs\nBiochemistry and Molecular Biology\nBiological Sciences\nChemistry\nMathematics and Statistics\nNeuroscience, Cell Biology, & Physiology\nPhysics\nPsychology\nInterdisciplinary Programs\nEarth and Environmental Sciences\nMicrobiology and Immunology\nDegrees and Programs\nThe Wright State University College of Science and Mathematics offers academic programs that span a variety of degree types and scientific disciplines. Whether you are seeking a bachelor\u2019s degree in statistics, a master\u2019s degree in microbiology and immunology, or a Ph.D. in human factors and industrial/organizational psychology, Wright State has a program that fits your interests and career goals. You can have confidence in our tradition of helping first-generation and underrepresented students and providing hands-on research opportunities and real-world experiences to students like you.\nBachelor's Degrees\nBiochemistry and Molecular Biology (B.S.)\nBiological Sciences (B.A.)\nBiological Sciences (B.S.)\nChemistry (B.S.)\n\u200bACS Certified (B.S.)\nChemistry Education Concentration (B.S.)\nDual Major (B.S.)\nEarth and Environmental Sciences (B.S.), Environmental Sciences Concentration\nMathematics (B.